    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "By treating the integrand as a reciprocal function, show that $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\frac{\\cos x}{1+\\sin x}\\,dx\\approx0.4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)\\approx0.4$.",
      "worked": "Let $f(x)=1+\\sin x$, so $f'(x)=\\cos x$. On $0\\le x\\le\\frac{\\pi}{6}$, $1+\\sin x>0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^{\\pi/6}\\frac{\\cos x}{1+\\sin x}\\,dx&=\\left[\\ln(1+\\sin x)\\right]_0^{\\pi/6}\\\\&=\\ln\\left(1+\\frac12\\right)-\\ln1\\\\&=\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)\\\\&\\approx0.4.\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
